abstract: >-
  Open educational resources for a one-day workshop for doctoral
  candidates and postdocs. The workshop examines generative AI through
  four lenses: scale and environment, representation, lifecycle and
  labour, and political economy. Participants then use the Liberating
  Structures Panarchy and an adapted Ecocycle Planning to find feasible
  changes in their own research. The materials include lesson pages,
  Reveal.js slide decks, printable worksheets, a facilitator guide, and
  a template for a responsible generative AI use statement.
keywords:
  - generative AI
  - AI ethics
  - research integrity
  - open educational resources
  - Liberating Structures
  - Panarchy
  - doctoral education
